<title>SWITZERLAND: Tietmeyer-lasting consolidation important for EMU.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer-lasting consolidation important for EMU.</headline>
<dateline>INTERLAKEN, Switzerland 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer said on Wednesday it was important for prospective members of Europe's planned monetary union to achieve enduring consolidation of their public finances.</p>
<p>Asked by reporters if it was decisive for a country to meet the 3.0 percent deficit criterion exactly, Tietmeyer said, &quot;We will look where a country is coming from, where it stands and what its course is for the future.&quot;</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
